# App color theme

LinkUp uses a **single three-color theme** across the whole app. Do not use the light/grey/blue palette from design mockups or wireframes.

## Palette

- **Background:** Black (`AuthTheme.background`)
- **Primary text / borders:** White (`AuthTheme.primary`)
- **Secondary text (labels, hints):** White at 60% opacity (`AuthTheme.secondary`)
- **Accent (buttons, links, focus):** Cyan `#00D4FF` (`AuthTheme.accent`)

## Where it’s defined

Colors are in **`LinkUp/Authentication/AuthTheme.swift`**. Use `AuthTheme.background`, `AuthTheme.primary`, `AuthTheme.secondary`, and `AuthTheme.accent` for all screens (auth, messages, polls, settings, etc.), not system greys or mockup colors.

## Design mockups

When implementing screens from the LinkUp Design image (or any mockup), follow the **layout and structure** from the design, but always apply the **AuthTheme** colors above. Ignore mockup colours (e.g. white backgrounds, grey text, blue accents from the image).
